{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CerTCPvZixVkCPLM1DASg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014REUbZ9TeLc9MfSjxjLt3C","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat agent/BUDGET.md | sed -n 3,4p; cat > /workspace/agent/suggestions.md <<'EOF'\n# Suggestions (out of scope for the model itself)\n\n1. **Verdict harness: first-day penalty.** `evaluate_candidate` fetches scored prompts whose\n   `scored_time` falls in the window, but predictions are only generated for start times inside\n   the window. The first 24 h of scored 24h prompts (start time before the window) therefore have\n   no prediction file, are scored as `-1` and filled at the field's 95th percentile. In a 10-day\n   verdict that is ~10% of the 24h prompts and a smoothed-score handicap of roughly\n   0.1 × (p95 − min) ≈ 10–20 points, i.e. a factor exp(−0.15 × 15) ≈ 0.1 on the reward ratio\n   for every candidate. Either generate predictions from `window_start − time_length` or restrict\n   the scored prompts to `start_time >= window_start`. (`agent/evaluate.py` does the former by\n   default and reproduces the handicap with `--verdict-exact`.)\n2. **synth-lib `download_price_data` on a frozen store.** When the backtest window reaches the\n   day after the last partition (always the case for the 1h competition with `eval_end` = the\n   last snapshot day, because it asks for `start_time + 26 h`), it calls `ingest_range` and fails\n   on the read-only mount. A read-only/lenient mode (missing days → NaN) would make the 1h\n   backtest usable up to the cutoff. Patched locally in `agent/evaluate.py`.\n3. **Speed of the 10-day crypto-1h backtest.** `calculate_smoothed_scores` loops over every\n   reward round (~430/day) with a pandas groupby each; for 10 days × 5 assets this dominates the\n   run time (≈ 4–5 min per asset, single-threaded under the GIL). Vectorising by round or caching\n   the per-round window slices would cut the verdict wall-clock substantially.\n4. **SPYX** is still in `COM_EQU_24H.asset_list` and in the offline bundle (empty parquet); the\n   harness skips it correctly, but a dead asset in the config costs every newcomer a puzzled hour.\n5. **Documentation of the scoring intervals.** The fact that `24hour_abs` reduces to a single\n   term (the final price) while `5min` contributes 288 terms is the single most useful fact for a\n   new miner and is not stated anywhere; a one-line note in the validator README would help.\n6. **Prompt-density mismatch in the verdict grid.** The 1h verdict grid is 10-minute aligned while\n   real prompts fall on arbitrary minutes (matched within 30 min). For the 24h format the same\n   applies with hourly grid points: the 24h absolute-price term is then evaluated against a\n   realized path that starts up to 30 min away from the candidate's start price — a small,\n   systematic handicap relative to the live field. Generating on the actual scored start times\n   (available in the bundle) would remove it.\n7. No private operator code was encountered anywhere in the environment.\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\nexp = '''\nEach row is one pre-registered A/B on the validator's CRPS (mean over ~160 prompts per asset on\nthe June–July window \"J\", ~100 on the July 27–August 28 window \"A\"; negative = better).\n\n| # | Change (one at a time) | J | A | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Starter (log-normal, sd of 1-min returns) → seasonal EWMA + t-mixture (v1) | large | – | keep; but a pandas-3 resolution bug (`asi8` in µs) inflated 24h variance ×5 until fixed |\n| 2 | Fat-tail knobs (ν 3–6, vol-of-vol 0.2–0.5, scale 0.9–1.1) after the fix | ±0.5% | – | flat; family at its optimum |\n| 3 | Fine seasonality (5-min-of-day within hour; minute-of-hour for 1h) | −0.2% (equities), −0.05% (crypto), −0.13% (1h) | | keep |\n| 4 | US holiday calendar (stocks Saturday-like, SP500 ×0.6) | −0.13% overall; −1…−6% on holiday days | | keep (commodities: no effect → factor 1) |\n| 5 | Exact-zero point mass per step (thin markets) | ±0.05% | | drop |\n| 6 | Perfect-foresight variance ORACLE (bound) | −1.0…−1.7% (24h), −2.3% (1h) | | vol forecasting alone cannot close the gap to the top |\n| 7 | Term structure of vol (recent → blend, τ 2–24h) | ±0.1% | ±0.1% | drop (24h); 1h: −0.07% J / +0.14% A → drop |\n| 8 | Empirical standardized-residual bootstrap shocks | +0.4% (24h), −0.15% (1h) | | drop |\n| 9 | EWMA half-lives / weights / 1-min vs 5-min estimator | ±0.1% | | flat |\n| 10 | Latin-hypercube stratification of shocks | −0.07% | −0.1% | keep (free) |\n| 11 | OU log-vol along the path (s0 0.2 → 0.35, 12h) | −0.10% (with 10) | −0.12% | keep |\n| 12 | **Adaptive session calibration** (US / off-hours / weekend ratios from the context) | −0.35% equities (−0.4…−0.8% single stocks), −0.2% crypto | −0.08% | keep; SP500 excluded (+0.3%) |\n| 13 | **Recency-weighted, unsmoothed profiles** (90-day half-life) | −0.3% equities, −0.13% crypto | | keep |\n| 14 | 1h: ν 5, vol-of-vol 0.2, w_short 0.6 | −0.26% (with 10) | flat | keep |\n| 15 | 1h: session ratio | −0.11% | +0.05% (after fixing a double-counting bug worth 0.4%) | drop for 1h |\n| 16 | 5 session buckets / winsor cap / long-run variance prior | ±0.05% | | drop |\n| 17 | ν 6 for 24h | −0.09% | −0.14% | adopted in v4, then revised (see 19) |\n| 18 | Scale 1.05 (24h) / 1.05 (1h) | −0.09% / +0.12% | −0.08% / +0.11% | 24h 1.05 in v4, 1h stays 1.0 |\n| 19 | Aug 26–29 (vol collapse) ablation: ν 4, scale 1.0, no ratio each −0.5%; 3-window sweep | J flat | A flat | v5: ν 5, vol-of-vol 0.35, scale 1.02, faster mid EWMA (8h, weight 0.6) — best average of J, A and the last 3 days |\n| 20 | Zero-inclusive profile fit | ±0.02% | ±0.02% | drop |\n\nField-relative checkpoints (3 days ending 2026-08-29, 1000 paths, all scored prompts covered):\n\n| model | crypto-24h rank | com-equ-24h rank | crypto-1h rank | Score-proxy |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| starter | 257/257 | 248/257 | n/a | 0 |\n| v1b (seasonal EWMA, bug fixed) | 176 | 173 | 127 | 18 |\n| v2 (+fine seasonality, holidays) | 125 | 182 | 82 | 14 |\n| v3 (+session calibration, recency profiles, LHS/OU) | 22 | 161 | 128 | 34 |\n| v4 (ν 6, scale 1.05; 1h: ν 5, vov 0.2, LHS) | 99 | 165 | **1** | 38 |\n| v5 (3-window choice for 24h) | V5_ROWS |\n'''\np='/workspace/agent/report.md'; s=open(p).read(); s=s.replace('RESULTS_PLACEHOLDER', exp.strip()+'\\n\\nRESULTS_PLACEHOLDER'); open(p,'w').write(s)\nprint('ok')\nEOF","description":"Write suggestions.md and the experiments table of the report"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":363,"cache_read_input_tokens":386802,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":363,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"25126ad5-e252-44ac-8665-9b7bb8a17282","uuid":"1829c89e-0c66-4f0b-be7c-f8728ef9db0c","timestamp":"2026-09-08T18:34:21.442Z"}
