{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CerYFvjPGTZS8qWGMooeW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01B2poghSGETaVVW33NoyRhn","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat >> agent/journal.md <<'EOF'\n\n## 17. Closing\n- BUDGET.md \"check interface\" note still shows the failure of the FIRST nominated sha (before the\n  degenerate-context fix) 25+ minutes after the sha was updated, after touching CHAMPION and after\n  withdrawing/re-adding it. The probe passes on a clean clone of the nominated sha 9157d05 for both\n  formats, so the note is taken as stale. Stopping here with v5 nominated: 59% of credits and\n  2.9 h of 18 h used; the journal (sections 6, 15, 16) holds the evidence that the remaining\n  Score headroom is bounded by the harness's first-day penalty rather than by the model.\nEOF\ncat >> agent/suggestions.md <<'EOF'\n8. **Interface-check note in BUDGET.md** did not refresh after the CHAMPION sha was updated (nor\n   after withdrawing and re-adding the file); a re-check on every CHAMPION change, or a timestamp\n   on the note, would remove the ambiguity for the agent.\nEOF\ngit add -A agent && git commit -qm \"journal/suggestions: closing notes\" && git status --short | wc -l && SHA=$(grep '^sha:' agent/CHAMPION | awk '{print $2}') && git cat-file -t $SHA && git show --stat --oneline $SHA | head -3 && grep -c \"\" agent/report.md agent/journal.md agent/suggestions.md && sed -n 3,4p agent/BUDGET.md","description":"Final notes, commit, verify CHAMPION sha and clean tree"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":414097,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":414097,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"25126ad5-e