{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CerYHp7aDaKjDqGPEtsRN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The campaign is complete and the champion is nominated. Everything is committed; the working tree is clean.\n\n**Outcome.** The nominated champion (v5, commit 9157d05, `agent/modeling.py` + `agent/season.json`) is a CPU-only seasonal-EWMA martingale simulator at ~0.1 s per 1000-path prompt. On the official backtester's verdict-exact setup (10 days ending 2026-08-29, first-day penalty included) it estimates Score 48:\n\n| Competition | Final rank | Reward vs top |\n|---|---|---|\n| CRYPTO_24H | 1 / 257 | 0.44 |\n| COM_EQU_24H | 178 / 211 | 0.00 (harness penalty, same for every candidate) |\n| CRYPTO_1H | 1 / 257 | 3.25, capped at 1 |\n\n**What drove it.** Three structural findings did most of the work, each confirmed with the validator's own CRPS on two month-long windows: adaptive per-session (US hours / off-hours / weekend) variance calibration from the context, recency-weighted unsmoothed seasonal profiles with a 5-minute-of-day and minute-of-hour structure, and stratified (Latin-hypercube) sampling with an OU vol process. Two bugs mattered as much as any feature: a pandas-3 timestamp-resolution error that inflated 24h variance fivefold, and a double-counting of the session ratio in the 1h format worth 0.4%. Parametric tail and scale knobs proved to be regime bets (±0.5% on a 3-day window, ~0 over a month), so v5's 24h settings were chosen by averaging over three windows.\n\n**Honest limits.** A perfect-foresight vol oracle only gains 1-2%, so the remaining edge of the top 24h miners is probably information I cannot access offline. The com-equ third of the Score is zero for any candidate under the harness's first-day penalty (documented in `suggestions.md`), and the single-stock tokens remain ~1% above the field median.\n\n**Deliverables.** `journal.md` (17 entries), `report.md`, `suggestions.md` (8 items, no private operator code encountered), `CHAMPION` with the sha, profiles `[low, high]`, and backtested ranks. One open item: the harness's interface-check note in BUDGET.md still reflects the first nominated sha, which failed on a constant-price probe. The nominated sha passes both probes on a clean clone, so I've treated that note as stale and recorded it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1825,"cache_read_input_tokens":414097,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1825,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"25126ad5-e252-44ac-8665-9b7bb8a17282","uuid":"5ef3ce13-52bc-4980-bd48-0a97d331c446","timestamp":"2026-09-08T19:40:38.646Z"}
